kunzite: the sandbox stand-in answers op 4, the container-path lookup (the containers kit's
implementation, patch 1003; design from 1002's boot-#62 dump). Op 4 is called by everyone —
cfprefsd alone 21,368 times in ten minutes on #62, retrying on the old ENOENT — with the struct
{ pid, 0 or pid-version, the caller's out-buffer, 0x400 } in both the _for_pid and the
_for_audit_token shapes (buf at word 2, length at word 3). Nothing ever calls the setters, so
there is no registry: the answer is the target pid's home, /private/var/root for uid 0 and
/private/var/mobile otherwise, copied into the caller's buffer; a pid that no longer exists
gets ESRCH. The strong definition replaces the weak stand-in that returned ENOENT. 1002's
argument dump now prints only with sweet_sbx_dump=1 in the boot-args, so the storm of console
lines goes with the storm of retries.

